   "executiveNarrative": "Czochralski crystal growth is a high-qualification manufacturing stage in which process discipline matters more than commodity volume. The commercial moat comes from low defectivity, repeatable crystal properties, customer qualification and the ability to operate expensive capacity at attractive utilisation. Artificial Intelligence and high-bandwidth memory can strengthen demand for advanced 300-millimetre wafers, but the node remains exposed to broader semiconductor inventory cycles and capital-spending discipline.",
